+      "from_key": "source-limited-status-20261010",
+      "to_existing_logical": "math:probability.open-problems:p0288-pollett-rank-two-limit-kernel-refuted",
+      "kind": "cites",
+      "rationale": "From: \"The supplied campaign already contains a candidate refutation of the rank-one polynomial-limit assertion for a lambda-transient killed chain. Its source and formula were rechecked here; independent audit and novelty remain unverified. Foley-McDonald arXiv:1709.07578v1 is a prior-art lead, not an established identification with this continuous-time example.\" To: \"[campaign status: candidate_full_solution - author-checked, unrefereed] Pollett's Section 2 conjecture (ii) asks whether, for a lambda-transient irreducible countable transient class with almost sure absorption, every finite strictly positive limit of t^a e^{lambda t} p_t(i,j) must factor as A x_i m_j. Our result (id P0288, 2026-09-08): NO. Take the nearest-neighbour continuous-time walk on Z (rate 1 each side), killed at rate kappa everywhere plus an extra rate v at the origin. The class is lambda-transient with lambda = kappa, and t^{3/2} e^{kappa t} p_t(i,j) tends to [(|i| + 2/v)(|j| + 2/v) + i j] / (4 sqrt pi). The i j term makes the limit a rank-two form - its 2x2 minor on rows and columns {0,1} equals (2/v)^2/(16 pi) > 0 for every v - so no rank-one A x_i m_j factorisation exists; the reason is structural, a chain with two ends carries one degree of freedom per end. Verification as the source words it: the Feynman-Kac semigroup was solved directly at t = 100, 400, 1600, 6400, and against the claimed limits 0.141047, 0.282095, 0.705237, 0.423142 for (i,j) = (0,0), (0,1), (1,1), (1,-1) at v = 2 the computed values converge monotonically to 0.141010, 0.282004, 0.705018, 0.422932, with the minor formed from the measured entries 0.019879 against the predicted 0.019894. PRIOR ART WARNING carried in the ledger row itself: Foley and McDonald published a discrete two-end construction from which the same continuous-time obstruction follows, so treat this as confirmed mathematics and probably known. continuous-time nearest-neighbour walk on Z at rate 1 each side killing rate kappa everywhere plus extra rate v at the origin lambda = kappa\". "
